Description: NETINSIGHT APT repository sources, signing key, and cinematic installer
 This package installs the GPG keyring at
 /etc/apt/keyrings/netinsight-archive-keyring.gpg and registers
 https://dkg-netinsight.github.io/apt-repo/ as an APT source for the
 detected Ubuntu codename (jammy or noble).
 .
 Modeled on the zabbix-release pattern. The sources.list entry is
 materialised by the postinst (codename auto-detected via
 /etc/os-release) so a single binary serves both supported releases
 without dpkg conffile contention on upgrade.
 .
 Starting with 1.0.0-55, this package also ships the Tier-1 cinematic
 installer entrypoint /usr/sbin/netinsight-install plus its supporting
 Python package /usr/share/netinsight/installer/.  Placing them here
 (rather than in netinsight-common as in 1.0.0-54) allows the canonical
 install sequence to be only TWO commands:
 .
   wget …netinsight-release_1.0.0-55+ubuntuXX.04_all.deb
   dpkg -i netinsight-release_1.0.0-55+ubuntuXX.04_all.deb
   netinsight-install
 .
 The cinematic UI (banner + animated workflow + 8-stage progress +
 summary card with QR) renders from frame 1, with all apt/dpkg/pip
 output suppressed to /var/log/netinsight/install.log.  python3-rich
 and qrencode are dependencies of this package so the renderer is
 already present when `dpkg -i` completes; the postinst pulls them via
 apt-get when needed.  figlet, boxes, and lolcat are recommended as a
 degraded ASCII fallback path on terminals that cannot render rich.

